award_description:
This scholarship has been established by Dr. Norman W. McLeod, FRSC, in honour of his wife, Irene Marguerite McLeod. It will be awarded annually, if suitable candidates exist, for postgraduate research in the following, in order of preference:
Bituminous materials, including recycling;
Flexible pavement design;
Any phase of land transportation by vehicles, excluding railroads
The recipient will normally be a graduate student in the Transport Group of the Department of Civil & Environmental Engineering.

eligibility_selection_criteria:
Full-time graduate students registered in Biology in the master's or doctoral program in the Department of Biology in the Faculty of Science;
Selection to be based on academic achievement (minimum cumulative average of 80% or equivalent over the last two full-time academic years) and students conducting research in zoology;
Application is not required;
Department of Biology will identify candidates and select recipients normally each Winter (March/April).

Graduate students registered full time in the Master's of Computational Mathematics program. Recent graduates within the past 2-3 academic terms may also be considered.
Selections will be made based on various factors that may include some or all of the following:
Academic excellence (minimum cumulative average of 80% or equivalent);
Demonstrated overall performance based on the quality and presentation of student's research;
Outstanding performance as a graduate teaching assistant (GTA) as determined through feedback received from surveys.
The Computational Mathematics Director and the Graduate Committee of the Computational Mathematics program will select recipients annually.

Graduate students currently registered full time in the Master of Data Science and Artificial Intelligence (MDSAI) and the Master of Mathematics in Data Science (MMath in DS) programs. Recent graduates within the past 2-3 academic terms may also be considered.
Selection will be made based on various factors that may include some or all of the following:
academic excellence (minimum cumulative average of 80% or equivalent);
demonstrated research ability or potential;
student leadership and/or best co-op reports
The Data Science Graduate Program Director(s) and the Awards subcommittee of the Data Science program will select the recipients annually.
